---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Optimal Transport & Colour Transfer - François Pitié" currentSection="research">
  <div class="post">
    <header class="post-header mb-8">
      <div class="mb-2">
        <a href="/research" class="text-xs font-mono text-[var(--theme-link)] hover:text-[var(--theme-accent)]">&larr; back to research</a>
      </div>
      <h1 class="post-title">Optimal Transport &amp; Colour Transfer</h1>
      <p class="desc text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1.5 pb-3 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)]">
        Probability density transfer and Monge–Kantorovich optimal transport for automated colour grading.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-10">
      <!-- Hero Visual -->
      <div class="rounded overflow-hidden border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)] shadow-xs">
        <img 
          src="/images/colourtransfer.jpg" 
          alt="Colour Transfer: Original, Target Palette, and After Transfer" 
          class="w-full h-auto object-cover"
        />
        <div class="p-3 text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] border-t border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/70">
          <strong>Figure:</strong> Colour transfer — (left) original image, (centre) target colour palette image, (right) resulting image after continuous distribution transfer.
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Overview -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-[var(--theme-fg)] leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-light tracking-tight text-[var(--theme-heading)] pb-1.5 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)]">
          Overview
        </h2>
        <p>
          Colour transfer is the process of adjusting the colour palette of an image or video sequence so that it matches the appearance of a reference image. In film post-production, matching shots taken at different times or under different lighting has traditionally required careful, manual grading.
        </p>
        <p>
          The mathematical challenge is to find a mapping in 3D colour space that aligns the colour distribution (PDF) of a source image with that of a target, without causing artefacts like colour banding or washing out natural film grain.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- PDF Transfer & MatchGrade -->
      <section class="space-y-3 text-sm sm:text-base text-[var(--theme-fg)] leading-relaxed">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-light tracking-tight text-[var(--theme-heading)] pb-1.5 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)]">
          Probability Density Transfer &amp; MatchGrade
        </h2>
        <p>
          In work presented at ICCV 2005 and CVIU 2007, we proposed an exact, iterative solution to multi-dimensional probability density function transfer using one-dimensional Radon projections, as well as a closed-form linear mapping based on Monge–Kantorovich optimal transport. A post-processing step ensures that fine textures and film grain are preserved.
        </p>
        <p>
          The method was licensed to <strong>The Foundry</strong> and integrated into <strong>MatchGrade</strong> (part of the <em>Furnace</em> plug-in suite for Nuke), where it became a standard tool for shot matching in film visual effects.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2020, I published a survey paper in <em>IET Computer Vision</em> reviewing the development of colour transfer methods over the preceding 15 years.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Open Source Code & Resources -->
      <section class="p-4 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/40">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--theme-heading)] mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
          <i class="fa-brands fa-github text-base"></i>
          Code &amp; Tools
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--theme-muted)] mb-3 leading-relaxed">
          Reference MATLAB implementation of the iterative N-dimensional PDF transfer algorithm and the linear Monge–Kantorovich mapping.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <a 
            href="https://github.com/frcs/colour-transfer" 
            target="_blank" 
            rel="noopener noreferrer" 
            class="pub-btn"
          >
            frcs/colour-transfer on GitHub &rarr;
          </a>
          <a 
            href="https://www.foundry.com" 
            target="_blank" 
            rel="noopener noreferrer" 
            class="pub-btn"
          >
            The Foundry MatchGrade &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Publications -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-light tracking-tight text-[var(--theme-heading)] pb-2 border-b border-[var(--theme-border)] mb-4">
          Key Publications
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              Advances in colour transfer
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              IET Computer Vision, 14(6):304–322, 2020.
            </div>
            <div class="mt-2">
              <a href="https://doi.org/10.1049/iet-cvi.2020.0076" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-link)] hover:text-[var(--theme-accent)] hover:underline">
                DOI: 10.1049/iet-cvi.2020.0076 &rarr;
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              Automated colour grading using colour distribution transfer
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié, A. Kokaram, and R. Dahyot
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              Computer Vision and Image Understanding (CVIU), 107(1-2):123–137, 2007.
            </div>
            <div class="mt-2">
              <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cviu.2006.11.011" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-link)] hover:text-[var(--theme-accent)] hover:underline">
                DOI: 10.1016/j.cviu.2006.11.011 &rarr;
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              The linear Monge-Kantorovitch linear colour mapping for example-based colour transfer
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié and A. Kokaram
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              4th European Conference on Visual Media Production (CVMP), London, 2007.
            </div>
            <div class="mt-2">
              <a href="https://doi.org/10.1049/cp:20070083" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-link)] hover:text-[var(--theme-accent)] hover:underline">
                DOI: 10.1049/cp:20070083 &rarr;
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="p-3.5 rounded border border-[var(--theme-border)] bg-[var(--theme-card)]/20">
            <div class="font-semibold text-sm text-[var(--theme-heading)] leading-snug">
              N-Dimensional Probability Density Function Transfer and its Application to Colour Transfer
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-1">
              F. Pitié, A. Kokaram, and R. Dahyot
            </div>
            <div class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-muted)] mt-0.5 italic">
              Tenth IEEE International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV), Beijing, China, 2005.
            </div>
            <div class="mt-2">
              <a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/ICCV.2005.166" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-xs text-[var(--theme-link)] hover:text-[var(--theme-accent)] hover:underline">
                DOI: 10.1109/ICCV.2005.166 &rarr;
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
